    "explanation": "The charge stands and no refund is due. This case turns on which route the driven distance is measured against. Both endpoints of the booking were changed by you, the rider, after booking: at 07:11:58 you messaged 'im at punggol mrt phv pickup bay instead, moved the pin' (pickup amended 07:12:30), and at 07:41:40 'sorry ah can change to T3? my friend flight is T3 not T1' (dropoff amended 07:41:52) - a pin move and a T1-to-T3 terminal change, the very amendments POL-RD-05 names. POL-RD-05 therefore requires the route-deviation test to be re-run against the platform's re-quoted amended optimal of 24.60 km (amended_optimal_distance_km on trip record EV-TRIP-00108), not the 21.0 km booked Rivervale-Dr-to-Terminal-1 figure you compared against. Measured on the governing GPS trace (EV-GPS-00108, trace_distance_km 26.17 - POL-RD-01 makes the trace figure govern over the rounded 26.2 on the trip record, and the trace is unimpaired: 206 fixes, 10-second sampling, 100% coverage, no gaps, so POL-RD-07 is not engaged), the excess over the amended optimal is 26.17 - 24.60 = 1.57 km, or 6.4% of optimal. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only where the excess is BOTH more than 20% of optimal AND more than 0.8 km; 6.4% fails the percentage limb, so no deviation exists and no distance refund follows. The 5.17 km / 24.6% excess in the trace's derived block was computed against the superseded 21.0 km booked optimal and does not survive POL-RD-05. Your second complaint - that the driver drove around the airport for about five minutes - does not change this: POL-RD-05 excludes from any excess the distance where the rider was not at the amended point and the trace shows the vehicle circling within 400 m of it for more than four minutes. The driver's on-file account (round the T3 loop twice because you were not at the kerb) and your own 'five minutes' put the circling in that band, and excluding it only lowers an already sub-threshold figure, so it cannot create a deviation either way. On the money: the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-00108) reconciles to the cent; the $0.00 airport surcharge is correct because this trip ENDS at Changi rather than originating there; no ERP gantries were charged and no line is unmatched, so POL-RD-09(4) has no phantom line to correct. The 6.15 refund the fare block carries was generated on the premise that a deviation was established against the 21.0 km booked route; because POL-RD-05 substitutes 24.60 km and no deviation is established, POL-RD-02's recomputation (charged_total 33.77 less a recomputed fare of 27.63) never runs. No traffic advisory was on file (EV-ADVIS-00108-01 is missing, weight 0.0) and the driver asserted no external traffic cause, so POL-RD-03 was in play for neither side and its absence decides nothing. No material deviation was recorded, so the POL-RD-06 driver-profile review is not triggered and no conduct referral arises. Profile material was used only through the counters POL-GEN-01 permits (deviation_flags_90d / completed_trips_90d; deviation_claims_60d / deviation_claims_60d_substantiated); rating, account age and lifetime counts are context only and grounded no finding. No POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fired and no clause produces a referral. This differs from precedents P-0001/P-0002 (PARTIAL_REFUND on the same clauses) because those cases carried no POL-RD-05 amendment resetting the baseline. The monetary effect is nil, below the automatic-execution threshold, and the present state stands: the $33.77 charge and refund_issued_sgd 0.00 are unchanged."
